-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 66: SUMMARY PROCEEDINGS FOR POSSESSION OF LAND (part roc12, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` unless its GIVETH says otherwise.
--   JUST TRUE    the thing holds as the Order states it.
--   JUST FALSE   the Order says no in its own words (a flat negative, a "where" or "unless" condition not met,
--                a period the text fixes).
--   NOTHING      the Order does not answer: it is silent, it limits a grant by its own wording, a bare "must"
--                has not been done, or an act the Order dates has not yet been done.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.


-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 66 -- Summary proceedings for possession of land`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- proceedings brought by originating application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7534 | 1. Where a person claims possession of land which the person alleges is occupied solely by a person or persons (not being a tenant or tenants holding over after the termination of the tenancy) who entered into or remained in occupation without the firstmentioned person’s licence or consent or that of any predecessor in title of the firstmentioned person, the proceedings may be brought by originating application in accordance with the provisions of this Order.
@ref O 66 r 1 (src:7534)
GIVEN `a person claims possession of land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person alleges that the land is occupied solely by a person or persons who entered into or remained in occupation without the person's licence or consent or that of any predecessor in title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any of those occupiers is a tenant holding over after the termination of the tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 1 the proceedings may be brought by originating application under this Order` MEANS
    IF    `a person claims possession of land`
      AND `the person alleges that the land is occupied solely by a person or persons who entered into or remained in occupation without the person's licence or consent or that of any predecessor in title`
      AND (NOT (`any of those occupiers is a tenant holding over after the termination of the tenancy`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person claims possession of land which the person alleges is occupied solely by a person or persons (not being a tenant or tenants holding over after the termination of the tenancy) who entered into or remained in occupation without the firstmentioned person's licence or consent ... the proceedings may be brought by originating application in accordance with the provisions of this Order"

