§§ `Rule 7 -- order for possession`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7562 | 7. —(1) A final order for possession in proceedings under this Order, except in case of emergency and with permission of the Court, must not be made less than 14 days after the date of service of the originating application. (2) An order for possession in proceedings under this Order must be in Form 95.
@ref O 66 r 7(1) (src:7562)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the final order for possession is made` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` IS A DATE
      `it is a case of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 7(1) the final order for possession may be made` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the date the final order for possession is made` LESS THAN `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done`
         THEN IF `it is a case of emergency` AND `the Court has given permission`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in case of emergency and with permission of the Court" lifts the bar and grants nothing (QA)
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A final order for possession ... must not be made less than 14 days after the date of service of the originating application"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar speaks only of an order made less than 14 days after service; the paragraph grants no right to an order made later

@ref O 66 r 7(1) (src:7562)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the final order for possession is made` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` IS A DATE
      `it is a case of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 7(1) a final order made on that date is barred` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the date the final order for possession is made` LESS THAN `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` AND (NOT (`it is a case of emergency` AND `the Court has given permission`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar reaches only an order made less than 14 days after service and not saved by emergency and permission

-- The earliest day a final order may be made without emergency and permission: 14 days after the date of service of the originating application.
-- A date cannot carry JUST FALSE, so the yes/no twins above ask whether an order made on a given day may be made or is barred.
-- src:7562 | 7. —(1) A final order for possession in proceedings under this Order, except in case of emergency and with permission of the Court, must not be made less than 14 days after the date of service of the originating application. (2) An order for possession in proceedings under this Order must be in Form 95.
@ref O 66 r 7(1) (src:7562)
GIVEN `the date of service of the originating application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 66 r 7(1) the earliest date for a final order for possession` MEANS `the date of service of the originating application` PLUS 14

@ref O 66 r 7(2) (src:7562)
`o 66 r 7(2) the form of the order for possession` MEANS "95"

@ref O 66 r 7(2) (src:7562)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form used` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 7(2) the order for possession is in the form the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in proceedings under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the form used` EQUALS `o 66 r 7(2) the form of the order for possession`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be in Form 95"; the Rule does not say what follows another form

