§§ `Rule 8 -- enforcement order for possession`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7565 | 8. —(1) A party may not, without the permission of the Court, file an application for an enforcement order to enforce an order for possession under this Order after the expiry of 3 months after the date of the order for possession. (2) An application for permission of the Court may be made without notice unless the Court otherwise directs.
@ref O 66 r 8(1) (src:7565)
`o 66 r 8(1) the period after which permission is needed` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 3
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

@ref O 66 r 8(1) (src:7565)
GIVEN `the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 8(1) the party may file the application for an enforcement order` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an enforcement order to enforce an order for possession under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the date the application is filed` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
         THEN IF `the Court has given permission`
              THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the permission of the Court" lifts the bar and grants nothing (QA)
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A party may not, without the permission of the Court, file an application ... after the expiry of 3 months after the date of the order for possession"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the bar speaks only of an application after the 3 months; the paragraph grants no right to file within them

@ref O 66 r 8(1) (src:7565)
GIVEN `the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 8(1) a filing on that date without permission is barred` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an enforcement order to enforce an order for possession under this Order"
    ELSE IF `the date the application is filed` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND (NOT (`the Court has given permission`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar reaches only a filing after the 3 months and without permission

@ref O 66 r 8(2) (src:7565)
GIVEN `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 8(2) the application for permission may be made without notice` MEANS
    IF `the Court otherwise directs`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise directs"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:7566 | (3) The enforcement order for possession must be in Form 96.
@ref O 66 r 8(3) (src:7566)
`o 66 r 8(3) the form of the enforcement order for possession` MEANS "96"

@ref O 66 r 8(3) (src:7566)
GIVEN `the form used` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 8(3) the enforcement order for possession is in the form the Rule requires` MEANS
    IF `the form used` EQUALS `o 66 r 8(3) the form of the enforcement order for possession`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be in Form 96"; the Rule does not say what follows another form

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 9 -- setting aside an order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7568 | 9. The Court may, on such terms as the Court thinks just, set aside or vary any order made in proceedings under this Order.
@ref O 66 r 9 (src:7568)
GIVEN `the order was made in proceedings under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 66 r 9 the Court may set aside or vary the order on such terms as it thinks just` MEANS
    IF `the order was made in proceedings under this Order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any order made in proceedings under this Order"

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 66 -- the duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- The text names who must act and states no number of days, so no rule below has a WITHIN.

DECLARE `o 66 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 66 the claimant`
    `o 66 the Court`
    `o 66 a party`

DECLARE `o 66 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 66 include the note at the end of the originating application`
    `o 66 file the supporting affidavit with the originating application`
    `o 66 serve the originating application and the affidavit`
    `o 66 make a final order for possession less than 14 days after service without emergency and permission`
    `o 66 file an application for an enforcement order after 3 months without permission`

-- src:7538 | 3. An originating application filed under this Order must include the following note at the end of the originating application: “ Note : Any person occupying the premises who is not named as a defendant by this originating application may apply to the Court personally or by solicitor to be joined as a defendant. If a person occupying the premises does not attend personally or by solicitor at the time and place abovementioned, such order will be made as the Court may think just and expedient. ”.
@ref O 66 r 3 (src:7538)
`o 66 r 3 the claimant's duty to include the note` MEANS
    PARTY `o 66 the claimant`
    MUST `o 66 include the note at the end of the originating application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 66 the claimant` BECAUSE "the originating application filed under this Order did not include the prescribed note at its end"

-- src:7540 | 4. —(1) At the time of the filing of the originating application under this Order, the claimant must file a supporting affidavit stating — ( a )
-- src:7541 | the claimant’s interest in the land;
-- src:7542 | ( b )
-- src:7543 | the circumstances in which the land has been occupied without licence or consent and in which the claimant’s claim to possession arises; and
-- src:7544 | ( c )
-- src:7545 | that the claimant does not know the name of any person occupying the land who is not named in the summons.
@ref O 66 r 4(1) (src:7540-7545)
`o 66 r 4(1) the claimant's duty to file the supporting affidavit` MEANS
    PARTY `o 66 the claimant`
    MUST `o 66 file the supporting affidavit with the originating application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 66 the claimant` BECAUSE "the claimant did not file a supporting affidavit stating the matters required at the time of filing the originating application"

-- src:7548 | 5. —(1) Where any person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application, the originating application together with a copy of the supporting affidavit must be served on the person — ( a )
-- src:7549 | personally;
-- src:7550 | ( b )
-- src:7551 | by leaving a copy of the originating application and of the affidavit or sending them to the person at the premises; or
-- src:7552 | ( c )
-- src:7553 | in such other manner as the Court may direct.
@ref O 66 r 5(1) (src:7548-7553)
`o 66 r 5(1) the claimant's duty to serve the named occupier` MEANS
    PARTY `o 66 the claimant`
    MUST `o 66 serve the originating application and the affidavit`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 66 the claimant` BECAUSE "the originating application and a copy of the supporting affidavit were not served on the named occupier"

-- src:7562 | 7. —(1) A final order for possession in proceedings under this Order, except in case of emergency and with permission of the Court, must not be made less than 14 days after the date of service of the originating application. (2) An order for possession in proceedings under this Order must be in Form 95.
@ref O 66 r 7(1) (src:7562)
`o 66 r 7(1) the prohibition on an early final order for possession` MEANS
    PARTY `o 66 the Court`
    SHANT `o 66 make a final order for possession less than 14 days after service without emergency and permission`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 66 the Court` BECAUSE "a final order for possession was made less than 14 days after the date of service of the originating application, without an emergency and the Court's permission"

-- src:7565 | 8. —(1) A party may not, without the permission of the Court, file an application for an enforcement order to enforce an order for possession under this Order after the expiry of 3 months after the date of the order for possession. (2) An application for permission of the Court may be made without notice unless the Court otherwise directs.
@ref O 66 r 8(1) (src:7565)
`o 66 r 8(1) the prohibition on a late application for an enforcement order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 66 a party`
    SHANT `o 66 file an application for an enforcement order after 3 months without permission`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 66 a party` BECAUSE "an application for an enforcement order was filed after the expiry of 3 months after the date of the order for possession, without the Court's permission"
